ean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-two-sided-dyadic"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-two-sided-dyadic"],"id":"long.thm-two-sided-dyadic","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.9 (A conditional two-sided dyadic bound)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.9, p. 47, label thm:two-sided-dyadic","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Assume the following two conditions for every row $s\\ge5$:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n \\mathrm M\\text{ at }s&\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n 4\\,\\mathrm{rem}(s)-p_s^--4\\notin\\{-3,-2,-1\\},\\\\\n \\mathrm R\\text{ at }s\\text{ and }o_s\\le2^s\n &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad 4o_s+p_s^+\\le2^{s+2}.\n \\end{aligned}\n$$\nThen at every row $s\\ge5$,\n$$\n\\mathrm{rem}(s)\\le2^s\\quad\\text{or}\\quad o_s\\le2^s.\n$$\nThe first hypothesis concerns only middle transitions. The second concerns only right transitions at which the old overshoot is at most $2^s$. Neither condition is asserted here for the whole sequence.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-two-sided-dyadic","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-two-sided-dyadic","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-two-sided-dyadic%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.SeamTwoSidedDyadicCellEscape.twoSided%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-two-sided-dyadic%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.SeamTwoSidedDyadicCellEscape.twoSided%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.SeamTwoSidedDyadicCellEscape.twoSided"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256